      "text": "Ladies and gentlemen, it's an honor to address you at the 6th Artificial Intelligence for Information Accessibility Conference held in commemoration of the International Day for Universal Access to Information Organized by UNESCO. Today, I'm pleased to share with you my lecture on title Artificial Intelligence at the Service of Humanity. As we know, we're living in new contexts. We live in a time defined by exponential era. Here in Mexico, more than 100 million people are Internet users, representing the 80% of the population. In Latin America, the figure is around 81%. And there is another revalent fact. 59% of the users are already interacting with artificial intelligence tools. AI is not an accessory. It has become a community of cognitive, creative and analytical tools, what some authors describe",
