      "duration": 79.97,
      "text": "AI is not only a driver of productivity and international cooperation, but also is a feel of geopolitical, cultural and ethical disputes. We must never forget that every algorithm carries social implications, like from Russia, racial and gender basis, to the way it malls collective imaginaries, redefineness, rationality around efficiency, effaciently and profits, or even generates artificial identities and aesthetics. In this sense, AI is not neutral. It is an active agent of symbolic mediation. Against this risk, it is essential to imagine and implement AI as a tool for the common good. First, let us consider epistemic justice. The possibility that AI facilitates more equitable access to knowledge, incorporating indigenous, female, rural and non-western ways of knowing.",
