      "duration": 81.03,
      "text": "The first is critical and sustainable digital literacy. Citizens must be equipped to read algorithms critically, to understand their environmental footprint, and to question the values embedded in technological design. The second is the adaptability and continuous learning. The speed of change requires to constantly learn, crossing disciplinary boundaries and integrating technological, ethical, communicative, and humanistic knowledge. The third is the rehumanization of the digital bound. We must never forget that behind every data set and every interface, there are people with dignity, histories, and context deserving of respect. Boiled in these competencies means fostering responsibility and responsible social-technical imagination. Care for oneself and other, on AI's limits and the promotion of an active algorithm citizenship.",
