      "text": "This implies overcoming knowledge fragmentation by articulating scientific, technical, and humanistic perspective. All of this plays before us enormous ethical and anthropological changes. AI confronts us with fundamental rights, the rights to truth, to identity, to privacy, to equality and non-discrimination, to cultural access, and to personal data protection. It also requires us to protect the most vulnerable people with disabilities, older adults, and marginalized communities, and topologically, the challenge is to resist the humanization, and remain faithful to ourselves and to our communities, to foster cultures of hope and sharing, and to sustain genuine encounters with the others. In short, ethics must guide the technological development, AI cannot be an end in itself.",
